{
    "output": {
        "claim": "The European Central Bank has officially announced the complete phasing out of physical Euro banknotes by the end of 2025, moving to a mandatory digital-only currency system to track every citizen's spending in real-time.",
        "final_decision": "fake",
        "credibility_score": 0.1,
        "final_justification": "The claim is fake as all its core components are contradicted or not supported by the provided evidence. The European Central Bank (ECB) has not announced the complete phasing out of physical Euro banknotes by the end of 2025. Instead, the digital euro is planned to complement, not replace, physical cash, with a projected launch in the second half of 2029. Furthermore, the ECB has stated intentions to ensure privacy with the digital euro, contradicting the idea of a system designed to track every citizen's spending in real-time.",
        "sources_for_investigation": [
            "https://www.euronews.com/business/2025/08/20/cash-is-king-why-does-the-eurozone-need-a-digital-euro",
            "https://www.usnews.com/news/articles/2016-05-06/can-europe-thwart-criminals-and-terrorists-by-phasing-out-big-bills",
            "https://www.reuters.com/business/finance/ecbs-cipollone-says-digital-euro-will-protect-european-banks-card-schemes-2026-02-18/",
            "https://www.ft.com/content/b0602271-cd43-4a6e-a96d-c8166a05d040",
            "https://cepr.org/voxeu/columns/digital-euro-awareness-adoption-and-household-portfolios",
            "https://cepa.org/article/europe-embraces-digital-currency-not-the-us/",
            "https://www.ft.com/content/99a7b61b-c5df-4794-8c5f-2e3acd291333",
            "https://www.cato.org/free-society/fall-2024/cbdc-spells-doom-financial-privacy",
            "https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/cbdctracker/",
            "https://www.bis.org/publ/qtrpdf/r_qt2003j.htm",
            "https://carnegieendowment.org/research/2021/08/chinas-digital-yuan-an-alternative-to-the-dollar-dominated-financial-system",
            "https://www.bruegel.org/analysis/european-union-should-embrace-decentralised-finance-and-make-it-safe"
        ],
        "subclaim_results": [
            {
                "subclaim": "Announced(European_Central_Bank, Phasing_Out_Physical_Euro_Banknotes) ::: Verify that the European Central Bank announced the phasing out of physical Euro banknotes.",
                "classification": "not_supported",
                "justification": "Evidence indicates the ECB plans for a digital euro to complement physical cash, not to phase it out. Statements from ECB officials emphasize preserving the benefits of cash and complementing it with a digital form."
            },
            {
                "subclaim": "Completion_Date(Phasing_Out_Physical_Euro_Banknotes, End_of_2025) ::: Verify that the complete phasing out of physical Euro banknotes is by the end of 2025.",
                "classification": "not_supported",
                "justification": "The only evidence regarding a phasing out date refers to the 500-euro banknote around the end of 2018, not all physical Euro banknotes by the end of 2025."
            },
            {
                "subclaim": "Announced(European_Central_Bank, Move_to_Mandatory_Digital-Only_Currency_System) ::: Verify that the European Central Bank announced a move to a mandatory digital-only currency system.",
                "classification": "not_supported",
                "justification": "Evidence consistently states that the digital euro is intended to supplement physical cash, not replace it with a mandatory digital-only system. The planned launch of the digital euro is in the second half of 2029, not 2025."
            },
            {
                "subclaim": "Purpose(Mandatory_Digital-Only_Currency_System, Track_Every_Citizen's_Spending_in_Real-Time) ::: Verify that the mandatory digital-only currency system is to track every citizen's spending in real-time.",
                "classification": "not_supported",
                "justification": "While some sources discuss the potential for CBDCs to enable tracking, the ECB has stated that the digital euro will ensure privacy by separating citizens' identity from payment data. There is no evidence that the ECB's announced purpose is to track every citizen's spending in real-time, and the premise of a \"mandatory digital-only currency system\" is also not supported."
            }
        ]
    }
}

{
    "output": {
        "claim": "NASA recently admitted in a leaked internal memo that the 1969 moon landing was filmed in a high-security studio in Nevada because the radiation belts were too deadly for astronauts to survive the journey through deep space.",
        "final_decision": "fake",
        "credibility_score": 0.1,
        "final_justification": "Evidence strongly contradicts the claim that NASA admitted the 1969 moon landing was filmed in a studio. The acting administrator of NASA, Sean Duffy, publicly reaffirmed that the moon landing did take place. There is also no evidence to support the claim that NASA admitted the radiation belts were too deadly for astronauts to survive. While radiation in space is a concern, Apollo missions were designed to minimize exposure by carefully planned trajectories and the speed of travel through the Van Allen belts, with the spacecraft providing some shielding. Astronauts considered this an acceptable risk, and NASA has not stated the belts were too deadly to survive.",
        "sources_for_investigation": [
            "https://www.pbs.org/newshour/science/apollo-landing-footage-would-have-been-impossible-to-fake-a-film-expert-explains-why",
            "https://www.theguardian.com/science/2019/jul/10/one-giant-lie-why-so-many-people-still-think-the-moon-landings-were-faked",
            "https://www.theparisreview.org/blog/2019/07/18/how-stanley-kubrick-staged-the-moon-landing-and-other-stories/",
            "https://fullfact.org/online/buzz-aldrin-moon-landing-interview/",
            "https://www.snopes.com/list/myths-about-the-moon-landing/",
            "https://www.nytimes.com/2025/10/31/us/politics/kim-kardashian-moon-landing-nasa-sean-duffy.html",
            "https://science.nasa.gov/biological-physical/stories/van-allen-belts/",
            "https://answersingenesis.org/astronomy/did-man-really-land-on-moon/",
            "https://slate.com/technology/2019/07/19/moon-landing-fake-american-conspiracy-why.html"
        ],
        "subclaim_results": [
            {
                "subclaim": "Admitted(NASA, 1969_Moon_Landing_Filmed_In_High-Security_Studio) ::: Verify that NASA admitted the 1969 moon landing was filmed in a high-security studio.",
                "classification": "not_supported",
                "justification": "The acting administrator of NASA, Sean Duffy, publicly reaffirmed that the 1969 moon landing did, in fact, take place, directly contradicting any claim of an admission that it was faked in a studio."
            },
            {
                "subclaim": "Admitted(NASA, Radiation_Belts_Too_Deadly_For_Astronauts_To_Survive_Journey_Through_Deep_Space) ::: Verify that NASA admitted the radiation belts were too deadly for astronauts to survive the journey through deep space.",
                "classification": "not_supported",
                "justification": "While space radiation poses risks, NASA did not admit the radiation belts were too deadly. Apollo spacecraft trajectories were designed to minimize exposure by passing through the least dangerous parts of the inner belt quickly and avoiding the outer belt. The spacecraft also provided some protection, and astronauts considered the exposure an acceptable risk."
            }
        ]
    }
}

{
    "output": {
        "claim": "Secret documents from the United Nations reveal a plan to implement a global 'social credit score' by 2030, where individuals will be denied access to public transportation if their carbon footprint exceeds a monthly limit.",
        "final_decision": "fake",
